Consider the following ANSI C program (where `cur` captures the current value of the `static` variable `s` before the recursive call). The integer value printed by `main()` is ________.

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int compute(int n) {
    static int s = 2;
    if (n <= 0) return 0;
    s = s + n;
    int cur = s;
    return cur + compute(n - 1);
}
int main() {
    printf("%d", compute(4));
    return 0;
}
```

